  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v5.2.18 - building a decode capture can no longer fail a generation, whatever goes wrong. 5.2.17 made ONE guard inside TryCaptureAsync return null instead of throwing, and the next report was a different guard in the same method - 'attention slot count mismatch 44/49' - still killing every chat turn. Guards are exactly what gets added to over time, so catching them one at a time at the throw site is a losing shape; the contract now lives at the call site in GgufGenerator, beside the fallback. A capture is an OPTIMISATION and the fallback next to it is a complete, correct decode, so a capture that cannot be built is a performance outcome and never a failed answer. The failure is still reported loudly and capture is disabled for the session.",
